@startuml db-payment-service
title Database Diagram — payment_service_db (Payment Service)

hide circle
hide methods

top to bottom direction

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 8
skinparam ranksep 12
skinparam padding 1
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  HeaderBackgroundColor #FDEBD0
  BorderColor #E59866
  FontSize 10
  AttributeFontSize 9
}

class "payments" as payments {
  payment_id : uuid <<PK>>
  appointment_id : uuid <<logical FK → core_clinic, indexed>>
  amount : numeric(12,2)
  currency : varchar(10) = 'VND'
  status : varchar(20) = 'pending'
  provider : varchar(30) = 'vnpay'
  provider_txn_ref : varchar(100)
  order_info : text
  refund_amount : numeric(12,2)
  refunded_at : timestamp
  refund_status : varchar(20)
  refund_reason : text
  refund_requested_by : uuid
  refund_requested_at : timestamp
  refund_reviewed_by : uuid
  refund_reviewed_at : timestamp
  created_at : timestamp
  updated_at : timestamp
}

note bottom of payments
  Single-table service. appointment_id is a **logical**
  FK to core_clinic_service_db.appointments — no physical
  FK crosses databases. After a successful payment the
  service PATCHes appointment.payment_status on the
  Clinical EMR service over HTTP.

  Refund workflow (requested_by → reviewed_by →
  refunded_at) is tracked entirely in this table.
  Idempotency + VNPay IPN replay guard live in shared
  Redis (logical db 4), not in PostgreSQL.
end note

@enduml
